<!-- ========== 01 — HERO ========== -->
<section class="brique wrap" style="padding-top:40px">
  <p class="eyebrow center rv" style="margin-bottom:24px">If you flinch when you see your own face</p>
  <h1 class="center rv" style="max-width:640px;margin:0 auto 14px">I used to untag myself from every photo without looking — then I read one paragraph that made me angry no one had bothered to explain it to me in ten years. Now I <span class="rosa">walk past a mirror</span> without tilting my chin down.</h1>
  <p class="lede center rv" style="max-width:560px;margin:0 auto 16px">For ten years I thought my skin was the problem. It wasn't. It never had been. <span class="rosa-dk" style="font-weight:500">I had a face I no longer recognized as mine, and a feeling about it I couldn't name</span> — and no one had bothered to give me the words.</p>
  <figure class="shot rv" style="margin:14px auto;max-width:460px">
    <img src="{% if section.settings.hero_image != blank %}{{ section.settings.hero_image | image_url: width: 1400 }}{% else %}{{ 'hero.webp' | asset_url }}{% endif %}" width="928" height="1152" alt="A woman turned toward a bathroom mirror in soft morning light, her own face reflected back at her." fetchpriority="high">
  </figure>
  <p class="serif italic center rv" style="font-size:19px;color:var(--rosa-dk);max-width:480px;margin:0 auto">There's one paragraph below that took me ten years to find. Read it carefully. ↓</p>
</section>


<!-- ========== 02 — LEAD ========== -->
<section class="brique wrap">
  <div class="bigquote rv" style="margin-top:8px"><p>You're tired of reading these. I know. I read fifty before I gave up trying to find the one that wasn't lying to me.</p></div>

  <div class="reco stg">
    <div class="reco-line">I know the Wednesday morning mirror — the seconds before you decide whether today is bearable.</div>
    <div class="reco-line">I know the forty-five minutes of makeup that's actually just to come back down to baseline.</div>
    <div class="reco-line">I know the Zoom self-view you can't stop checking.</div>
    <div class="reco-line">I know the bathroom door after a meeting that didn't go well.</div>
    <div class="reco-line">I know the quiet untagging — every photo, without looking.</div>
    <div class="reco-line pay">I know the moment your face says something you weren't feeling — and you watched yourself be misread.</div>
  </div>

  <p class="serif italic center soft rv" style="font-size:18px;margin:24px 0">I'm not the only one who knows this. There are a lot of us.</p>
  <p class="serif italic center rosa-dk rv" style="font-size:19px;margin:18px 0">I know because I lived it. For ten years.</p>

  <p class="rv">What follows isn't another serum article. It isn't a sensitive-skin routine. It isn't a list of triggers to avoid. It's the explanation no one bothered to give me in the ten years I was asking for it.</p>

  <div class="statrow rv">
    <div><span class="n">21 months</span><span class="l">in a dermatology lab</span></div>
    <div><span class="n">43</span><span class="l">formulations tested</span></div>
    <div><span class="n">312 women</span><span class="l">panel · 8 weeks</span></div>
  </div>

  <p class="rv" style="margin-top:24px">Two years ago, someone did. <span class="rosa-dk" style="font-weight:500">I stopped looking for a cream. I started looking for a question.</span></p>

  <p class="serif italic center rosa-dk rv" style="font-size:20px;margin:16px auto;max-width:440px">Take the next five minutes. They were it.</p>

  <div class="pullquote rv" style="margin-top:18px">
    <p>Two years ago, at a café, a woman I'd never met leaned over.</p>
    <p>She asked me one question.</p>
    <p style="color:var(--rosa);font-weight:500">I haven't stopped thinking about it since.</p>
  </div>
</section>


<!-- ========== 03 — BACKGROUND STORY ========== -->
<section class="brique wrap">
  <h2 class="center rv" style="margin-bottom:10px">I wrote this letter for the woman whose Wednesday looks like this.</h2>
  <p class="center italic soft rv" style="margin-bottom:14px">Pick any three. If three are yours — the rest of this is too.</p>

  <div class="grid2 stg">
    <div class="mirror"><h4>The 7 AM mirror</h4><p>Where you decide what today will let you do.</p></div>
    <div class="mirror"><h4>The 45-minute makeup</h4><p>Not really makeup. Coverage.</p></div>
    <div class="mirror"><h4>The Zoom self-view</h4><p>The one you can't stop checking — even while someone is talking to you.</p></div>
    <div class="mirror"><h4>The family photo</h4><p>Where you're the one taking it. Where you got used to it.</p></div>
    <div class="mirror"><h4>The quiet untag</h4><p>Every photo. Without looking.</p></div>
    <div class="mirror"><h4>The bathroom door</h4><p>After the meeting that didn't go well. Sometimes longer than ten minutes.</p></div>
  </div>

  <p class="serif italic center rv" style="font-size:22px;margin:16px auto;max-width:460px">I checked off all six. Every morning. For ten years.</p>

  <div class="pullquote rv">
    <p style="font-size:clamp(18px,2.8vw,22px)">And the worst part wasn't checking them off. It was the feeling I couldn't put into words — that something had been missed, by every person I'd asked.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="founder rv">
    {%- if section.settings.margot_image != blank -%}<img class="founder-photo-img" src="{{ section.settings.margot_image | image_url: width: 120 }}" alt="Margot" width="56" height="56" loading="lazy">{%- else -%}<div class="founder-photo" title="Margot portrait (optional)">photo</div>{%- endif -%}
    <div>
      <div class="name">Margot</div>
      <div class="role">Not a dermatologist. Not a chemist.</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="rv">Me too. Reformulated after the fourth event — worse than what started.</p>
  <p class="rv"><strong>Esoterics.</strong> Twelve weeks. It didn't address the redness.</p>
  <p class="rv"><strong>Azelaic acid serums</strong> — The Ordinary, Stem Naturalcare. Both burned. I plateaued.</p>
  <p class="rv"><strong>IPL.</strong> Four sessions. $1,500 each. The third one made me red for a month.</p>
  <p class="rv"><strong>Niacinamide at 30%.</strong> Two weeks. It flared everything.</p>
  <p class="rv"><strong>Once gotten.</strong> Six months. It worked. Then I stopped — and within two months the flushing was back.</p>

  <p class="serif italic center rosa-dk rv" style="font-size:20px;margin:16px auto;max-width:460px">Twelve thousand dollars. Six tries. Each one answering the wrong question.</p>

  <div class="wash rv" style="margin:24px 0">
    <p style="margin:0;line-height:1.6">I was on a Zoom call with a client. I watched my own face in the bottom-right corner redden from collar to hairline while she was telling me about her contract renewal. I missed everything she said. I excused myself after that one. I closed my laptop at five and sat in the bathroom for twenty minutes. I just couldn't do it anymore.</p>
  </div>

  <p class="rv">That weekend I stopped looking for the next cream. I started looking for what was actually happening underneath. I read papers I didn't understand. I read Reddit threads at 2 AM. I posted in a forum.</p>
  <p class="rv">Three days later I was back at the café where I'd been writing for two years.</p>

  <p class="serif italic center rosa-dk rv" style="font-size:18px;margin:16px auto;max-width:520px">This was the first time I wished someone had written for me at twenty-eight. Or twenty-three. I'm writing it for you now.</p>

  <div class="ornament" style="margin:38px auto"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="3"/></svg></div>

  <p class="eyebrow muted rv" style="margin-bottom:12px">Tuesday · 2:47 PM</p>
  <h2 class="rv" style="text-align:left;margin-bottom:18px">The café where I'd been hiding for two years.</h2>

  <p class="dropcap rv">Before that morning, I had three creams in my bag — the ones I rotated to cover whichever flush was loudest. I was about to reach for the fourth when the woman at the next table leaned over. She told me later she hadn't planned to talk to me — she'd been watching me reach for tubes for two months, and that morning the watching had become its own thing she couldn't ignore.</p>

  <p class="rv">She asked me one question. <em>"How long have you been flushing like that?"</em> I told her. Ten years. She nodded slowly — the way someone does when you've just confirmed what they already knew.</p>

  <p class="rv">Her name was Helena. Retired vascular biologist. She'd been writing a novel at the same café for two years — which is how she'd been watching me reach for tubes.</p>

  <figure class="shot rv" style="margin:24px 0">
    <img src="{% if section.settings.cafe_image != blank %}{{ section.settings.cafe_image | image_url: width: 1400 }}{% else %}{{ 'cafe.webp' | asset_url }}{% endif %}" width="1376" height="768" alt="Overhead view of a small cafe table in afternoon light: two cups of coffee, a linen napkin, a few dried stems." loading="lazy">
  </figure>

  <p class="rv">She borrowed my napkin. She wrote on it for three minutes. Then she looked up.</p>

  <blockquote class="pullquote rv">
    <p>"Your face isn't broken."</p>
    <p>"It's been running the same five-step routine for a decade. And every product on your shelf has been treating one step — hoping the other four would follow."</p>
    <p>"They don't. They can't. That's not how it works."</p>
  </blockquote>

  <p class="serif italic center rosa-dk rv" style="font-size:20px;margin:24px 0">She turned the napkin around.</p>

  <div class="skip"><a href="#root" data-cta="03"><em>I've lived this</em> · take me to the answer <span class="arw">→</span></a></div>
</section>


<!-- ========== 04 — PROBLEM AGITATION ========== -->
<section class="brique wrap">
  <h2 class="rv" style="margin-bottom:20px">I walked home from the café trying not to look in shop windows.</h2>

  <figure class="shot rv" style="margin:24px auto 10px">
    <picture>
      <source media="(max-width:640px)" srcset="{% if section.settings.rosacea_mobile != blank %}{{ section.settings.rosacea_mobile | image_url: width: 1400 }}{% else %}{{ 'rosacea-mobile.webp' | asset_url }}{% endif %}">
      <img src="{% if section.settings.rosacea_desktop != blank %}{{ section.settings.rosacea_desktop | image_url: width: 1400 }}{% else %}{{ 'rosacea-desktop.webp' | asset_url }}{% endif %}" width="1376" height="768" alt="The same woman photographed at ages 25, 28, 31 and 34: her facial redness deepens across the four stages, from a faint flush on the cheekbones to persistent deep redness across the face." loading="lazy">
    </picture>
  </figure>
  <p class="rosacea-note">The same woman, ages 25 to 34. The flush deepens as you read: what an uninterrupted loop does to a face.</p>
  <p class="serif italic center soft rv" style="font-size:15px;margin:14px 0 30px">This was mine.</p>

  <p class="serif italic center rosa-dk rv" style="font-size:18px;margin-bottom:17px">That's when I started writing the other list. The one I'd never put on paper.</p>

  <div class="stg" style="max-width:560px;margin:0 auto">
    <div style="margin-bottom:24px;padding-left:20px;border-left:2px solid var(--rosa-lt)"><p class="serif rosa-dk" style="font-size:20px;font-weight:500;margin:0 0 4px">The mirror checks.</p><p class="soft small" style="margin:0">Three times before a meeting that doesn't even use video.</p></div>
    <div style="margin-bottom:24px;padding-left:20px;border-left:2px solid var(--rosa-lt)"><p class="serif rosa-dk" style="font-size:20px;font-weight:500;margin:0 0 4px">The phone front camera.</p><p class="soft small" style="margin:0">Opened just to confirm what I already know.</p></div>
    <div style="margin-bottom:24px;padding-left:20px;border-left:2px solid var(--rosa-lt)"><p class="serif rosa-dk" style="font-size:20px;font-weight:500;margin:0 0 4px">The Zoom self-view.</p><p class="soft small" style="margin:0">Has ruined more meetings than any client ever could.</p></div>
    <div style="margin-bottom:24px;padding-left:20px;border-left:2px solid var(--rosa-lt)"><p class="serif rosa-dk" style="font-size:20px;font-weight:500;margin:0 0 4px">The "are you okay?"</p><p class="soft small" style="margin:0">From a colleague who means well. Who doesn't know that's not what's happening.</p></div>
    <div style="margin-bottom:24px;padding-left:20px;border-left:2px solid var(--rosa-lt)"><p class="serif rosa-dk" style="font-size:20px;font-weight:500;margin:0 0 4px">The cancellation.</p><p class="soft small" style="margin:0">Written while looking at the photos on my fridge.</p></div>
    <div style="margin-bottom:24px;padding-left:20px;border-left:2px solid var(--rosa-lt)"><p class="serif rosa-dk" style="font-size:20px;font-weight:500;margin:0 0 4px">The foundation before the coffee.</p><p class="soft small" style="margin:0">Because the order matters.</p></div>
  </div>

  <div class="pullquote rv" style="margin-top:17px">
    <p style="font-style:normal;color:var(--ink);font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',serif;font-size:20px">None of these is the rosacea.</p>
    <p>These are the things I do because of it. <span style="color:var(--rosa);font-weight:500">And they weigh more than the flushing itself.</span></p>
  </div>

  <p class="serif italic center rosa-dk rv" style="font-size:18px;margin-top:15px">Helena had a shorter list. Five things, instead of mine.</p>
</section>


<!-- ========== 05 — ROOT CAUSE ========== -->
<section class="brique wrap" id="root">
  <p class="center italic soft rv" style="margin-bottom:16px">I leaned in. She'd written five things, in careful handwriting. For five seconds, I forgot how to breathe.</p>
  <p class="serif italic center rosa-dk rv" style="font-size:18px;margin-bottom:14px">You've felt this for years. You just didn't have the words.</p>

  <div class="pullquote rv"><p>She wasn't showing me five separate problems. She was showing me five steps of the same loop.</p></div>

  <p class="rv">Each step made the next worse. Every product I'd ever bought had been treating one — hoping the other four would follow. None of them could.</p>

  <figure class="shot rv" style="max-width:660px">
    <video class="loop-video" muted loop playsinline preload="none" poster="{% if section.settings.loop_poster != blank %}{{ section.settings.loop_poster | image_url: width: 1400 }}{% else %}{{ 'loop.webp' | asset_url }}{% endif %}" width="1376" height="768" data-src="{% if section.settings.loop_video != blank %}{{ section.settings.loop_video }}{% else %}{{ 'loop.mp4' | asset_url }}{% endif %}" aria-label="Cross-section of skin showing the five-step loop: the alarm, the nerve sensors, the dilating vessel, the leaking wall, and the fear loop returning to the start."></video>
    <figcaption>the loop · all five active</figcaption>
  </figure>

  <div class="lever rv"><div class="tag">01 · The Alarm</div><div class="sub">An immune system calling 911 when nothing was wrong.</div><p>Your immune system has a smoke detector. In healthy skin, it goes off when there's fire. In mine, it was going off when someone walked past with cologne. When the office got warm. When I drank a glass of wine. When I felt embarrassed. When I felt anything strong — even happy. Every trigger came through this one door.</p></div>

  <div class="lever rv"><div class="tag">02 · The Nerves</div><div class="sub">Set too sensitive after years of false alarms.</div><p>The nerves had been tuned too sensitive by years of false alarms. They fired at heat I wouldn't notice on my arm. At a thought, sometimes. Before anything had even happened.</p><p style="margin-top:12px">My face had started lying about me. I was calm — it flushed. I was steady — it screamed. People assumed I was nervous. People assumed I was embarrassed. <span id="neither" style="background:var(--rosa-wash);padding:2px 6px;border-radius:3px;color:var(--rosa-dk);font-weight:500">I was neither.</span> The link between what I felt and what my face said had been broken.</p></div>

  <div class="lever rv"><div class="tag">03 · The Door</div><div class="sub">A barrier that stopped keeping anything out.</div><p>Healthy skin has a wall around it. Mine had holes. Things other people would ignore — a colleague's perfume, the office AC, a "gentle" cleanser — went straight through and fed the alarm.</p></div>

  <div class="lever rv"><div class="tag">04 · The Wall</div><div class="sub">Vessels that learned to stay open.</div><p>The blood vessels in my cheeks had been opening for ten years. Closing slower each year. By thirty-four, the redness at 7 AM wasn't a flare. It was the baseline. Vessels that used to come back down — and stopped.</p></div>

  <div class="lever lever--five rv"><div class="tag">05 · The Loop Unwinds</div><div class="sub">What happens when the four above feed each other.</div><p>The fifth one isn't a separate thing. It's what the first four create when they run together. The alarm fires. The nerves overreact. The barrier lets more in. The vessels stay open. And every time it happens, the next time happens easier. The loop teaches itself.</p></div>

  <div class="pullquote rv" style="margin-top:15px">
    <p style="font-style:normal;font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',serif;color:var(--ink)">Five things. One loop.</p>
    <p style="font-style:normal;font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',serif;color:var(--ink)">Treat one — the other four keep running.</p>
  </div>

  <p class="center italic soft rv" style="margin-top:24px">I sat there reading the napkin twice. Then I exhaled.</p>

  <div class="skip"><a href="#product" data-cta="05"><em>I see the loop</em> · show me what stops it <span class="arw">→</span></a></div>
</section>


<!-- ========== 06 — MECHANISM ========== -->
<section class="brique wrap">
  <p class="rv">I looked at the five things on that napkin for a long time. Then I asked Helena the only question that mattered.</p>

  <div class="bigquote rv"><p>"If the loop runs through five things — what does it take to actually stop it?"</p></div>

  <p class="rv">She didn't hesitate.</p>
  <p class="rv">You have to <span style="background:#F6E3D6;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:3px;color:var(--rosa-dk);font-weight:500">deal with</span> all five at the same time. Not one at a time. Not one today and another next month. All five.</p>

  <p class="center" style="margin:22px 0 8px"><span class="mono-word scalein">Simultaneously.</span></p>

  <div class="pullquote rv" style="margin-top:20px"><p>Because the fifth one isn't something you deal with. It's what happens when the other four stop.</p></div>

  <figure class="rv" style="max-width:560px;margin:16px auto">
    <div style="background:var(--paper-2);border-radius:16px;padding:30px 18px 24px">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 400 168" width="100%" role="img" aria-label="Two gauges. Healthy skin: the needle rises then returns to baseline, over and over. Your skin: the needle only rises and stays up, a ratchet.">
